/home/dwalleck/.local/share/kiro-research/binaries/2.28.0/extracted/kirocli/bin/kiro-cli-chat: offset 99908960 copies 2 rows 21 overrides [{'offset': 99619718, 'summary': {'v3_prompt': {'treatment': 135}}, 'digest': '3d29b950321fdd59'}]
  background_execution: treatment=0 segment=internal channel=nightly :: Background execution for V3 sessions. One flag turns on both sides because, whenever it is on, the TUI sends backgroundExecution: { enabled: true } on session/new: the CLI display (shells chip, transcript rows for finished background processes, Ctrl+B to move a running command to the background, the Ctrl+G Shells monitor) and, from that setting, the agent's background layer itself (managed run_in_background, the move at the timeout, completion wakes, the control tool disclosed once a process runs, monitors, PTY). KAS reads no KIRO_ENABLED_FEATURES; a KAS reached without the CLI is enabled by its own operator override, KIRO_FEATURE_BACKGROUND_EXECUTION_ENABLED=true. Off, CLI and agent behave exactly as before the feature existed. Dark-shipped at 0% until the telemetry layer ramps it for internal users on the nightly channel; treatment_percent is the dial and the kill switch. Opt in anywhere with KIRO_ENABLED_FEATURES.
  c2s: treatment=100 segment=internal channel=nightly :: Code-to-Spec Explore agent and analysis pipeline. Internal nightly only; the rollout exposes Explore and the settings control, while chat.enableC2s enables the analysis tools.
  cloud_config: treatment=100 segment=all channel=None :: Cloud config: the consolidated /config panel, cloud/local source labels on config listings, and the launcher passing the stage-default cloud-config BFF endpoint to KAS for local V3 sessions. Turning this off hides the UI and stops the launcher supplying that stage default, so KAS makes no cloud-config calls unless the user explicitly sets a trusted-host CLOUD_CONFIG_ENDPOINT override (which applies regardless of the rollout). GA: ramped to 100% for ALL users on every channel; per-user activation stays governed by KAS's server-side AB_CLOUD_CONFIG entitlement, so non-entitled users see local-only sources. This flag is retained purely as the client-side kill switch: to darken the fleet, set treatment_percent to 0 in a follow-up release (config is compiled in); the immediate per-user lever is KIRO_FEATURE_CLOUD_CONFIG_ENABLED, an env override read by the KAS server (kiro-agent's feature-config provider), not by this crate.
  infra_safety: treatment=100 segment=internal channel=None :: ICECAP infrastructure-safety gate (monitor/enforce). Internal-only initially; launcher exports KIRO_INFRA_SAFETY_ROLLOUT_ENABLED and the TUI advertises the capability + honors the infraSafety settings only when enabled. Ramp via treatment_percent.
  kvim: treatment=100 segment=internal channel=None :: /kvim: Neovim in a pane above the fullscreen chat. The launcher includes kvim in KIRO_ENABLED_FEATURES and the TUI registers the /kvim command only when enabled. Internal users on every channel; dial treatment_percent to 0 to kill-switch. Opt in anywhere with KIRO_ENABLED_FEATURES.
  lite: treatment=100 segment=internal channel=None :: Lite TUI mode - all channels, Amazon employees only
  local_sandbox: treatment=100 segment=internal channel=nightly :: CLI LocalSandbox testing for internal nightly users on V3.
  memory: treatment=100 segment=internal channel=None :: Persistent agent memory and the /memories command. Ramped to all internal users on every channel; KAS's memory experiment still decides per-user eligibility.
  memory_controls: treatment=100 segment=internal channel=None :: KAS-only /memories controls: saved memory access and automatic-update defaults, plus record browsing (list, preview, detail). Ramped to all internal users on every channel; set treatment_percent to 0 to darken it.
  remote_changelog: treatment=100 segment=None channel=stable :: Remote changelog feed fetch on stable builds (prod CloudFront). Nightly always fetches from gamma unconditionally. GA: all stable users at 100%. To darken the fleet, set treatment_percent to 0 in a follow-up release (config is compiled in); the immediate per-user lever is KIRO_NO_REMOTE_CHANGELOG.
  remote_sandbox: treatment=100 segment=all channel=None :: Remote/cloud sandbox sessions (--cloud/--repo flags). Ramped to 100% for all users on every channel. Dial treatment_percent to 0 to kill-switch (re-darkens the flags in the next release).
  session_dashboard: treatment=100 segment=all channel=None :: Session dashboard: the /sessions browser, --sessions flag, and --resume-picker dashboard routing (v3). Generally available: every user on every channel. treatment_percent stays at 100 rather than ramping, because the single per-feature percent buckets internal users too — a partial percent would drop the feature for the internal cohort it was already ramped to. Dial treatment_percent to 0 to kill-switch (config is compiled in, so that ships in the next release). The surface is V3-only, but --sessions selects V3 itself, so the flag is not bounded by a separate engine choice; a user who saved or passed a non-V3 engine is told the dashboard needs V3 rather than being moved onto it.
  tangent: treatment=100 segment=all channel=None :: /tangent named side-conversations. Generally available; the launcher includes tangent in KIRO_ENABLED_FEATURES and the TUI registers the /tangent command only when enabled. Dial treatment_percent to 0 to kill-switch.
  test: treatment=100 segment=None channel=None :: Test experiment for unit tests
  test_internal_only: treatment=100 segment=internal channel=None :: Test experiment for unit tests (internal only)
  test_nightly_only: treatment=100 segment=internal channel=nightly :: Test experiment for unit tests (nightly channel only)
  trust_classifier_shadow: treatment=100 segment=internal channel=nightly :: Permission-classifier shadow mode: on every approval prompt the engine also asks the permission-classifier model for a verdict and records it beside the human's decision, never changing the prompt. Internal nightly only. Per-user opt-out is the trust.classifier.shadow setting; the launcher exports the combined decision as KIRO_TRUST_CLASSIFIER_SHADOW; today only the V2 engine reads it (V3 is planned). Dial treatment_percent to 0 to kill-switch.
  tui: treatment=50 segment=internal channel=None :: Gradual rollout of the new React/Ink TUI to replace legacy terminal UI
  v3_prompt: treatment=35 segment=internal channel=None :: Who is offered the V3 ease-in prompt. There is no feature that flips the default engine to V3 during the ease-in — the prompt is the only path — so a user is never defaulted onto V3 without being asked. Dialing this to 0 stops asking; answers already given are honored via the persisted chat.agentEngine setting.
  voice: treatment=100 segment=all channel=None :: Voice input mode - generally available to all users
  workflows: treatment=100 segment=all channel=None :: KAS dynamic workflows and TUI workflow management. Generally available to all users on the KAS engine; opt in via chat.enableWorkflows in /settings features.
